  "group": "mini",
  "prompt": "Is a ₱500 one-time courier payment to an individual subject to EWT?",
  "runtimeCommit": "6ce2d6fd613e7f3109022f5a0f5ea006e9122546",
  "answer": "### Issue Presented\nA ₱500 one-time courier payment to an individual is not subject to Expanded Withholding Tax (EWT) as it falls under the threshold for EWT applicability. According to Revenue Regulations No. 2-98, EWT applies to income payments that exceed certain amounts, and since this payment is below the threshold, it is not subject to EWT.\n\n### Legal Interpretation\n\nThe withholding obligation arises when a withholding agent makes payment to a resident income payee for a service subject to withholding under applicable revenue regulations.\n\n### Practical Application\n\nThe payor must withhold the applicable rate, remit to the BIR, and issue BIR Form 2307 (certificate of creditable withholding tax) to the payee.",
